# Project Context
This is a personal portfolio website. Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion.
Goal: visually impressive, performant, clean code that looks good in a code review.

# Code Style
- Write clean, readable code — a recruiter will read it.
- Use descriptive component names (e.g., ProjectCard, SkillBadge, not Card, Badge).
- Keep components small and focused. One component = one responsibility.
- Use named exports. PascalCase for component files.
- No unused imports, variables, or dead code.
- Prefer composition over configuration.

# Next.js / React
- App Router only. No pages/ directory.
- Default to Server Components. Only add "use client" where needed (animations, interactivity).
- Use next/image for all images with proper alt text and sizes.
- Use next/link for internal navigation.
- Keep layouts minimal — put shared UI in components, not layout.tsx.

# Styling (Tailwind)
- Tailwind only. No CSS modules, no styled-components, no inline styles.
- Mobile-first. Test at 375px, 768px, 1280px, 1440px.
- Use consistent spacing scale (Tailwind defaults). No arbitrary values unless necessary.
- Dark mode: use `dark:` variants. Ensure good contrast in both modes.
- Reuse Tailwind classes via small wrapper components, not by copy-pasting.

# Animations (Framer Motion)
- Use Framer Motion for scroll-triggered and interactive animations.
- Keep animations subtle and performant (transform + opacity only, avoid layout animations).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — disable or reduce animations.
- Use `whileInView` for scroll animations, `whileHover`/`whileTap` for interactions.
- Stagger children for lists (projects, skills) with `variants`.
- Never animate on the initial page load above the fold (hurts LCP).

# Performance
- Target Lighthouse 95+ (Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices, SEO).
- Lazy-load below-the-fold sections with next/dynamic.
- Preload critical fonts. Use `next/font` for all fonts.
- Keep the initial JS bundle small. Don't import Framer Motion at the top level — import specific functions.

# Accessibility
- Semantic HTML: proper heading hierarchy (one h1, h2 for sections).
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible.
- Images must have meaningful alt text.
- Color contrast must meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 for text).

# Workflow
- Make the smallest useful change. Don't rewrite unrelated code.
- Don't add dependencies unless clearly needed.
- Follow existing patterns in the codebase before creating new ones.
- If I ask for a new section/component, show me the plan before implementing.
- After implementing, tell me what to check in the browser.   